T*
(effects of passing mutable vs immutable objects.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Python passes arguments using 'call-by-object-reference'. The function parameter) Tj
T*
(receives a copy of the reference \(pointer\) to the actual object. If the object is) Tj
T*
(IMMUTABLE \(int, float, str, tuple\), modifying the parameter inside the function rebinds) Tj
T*
(the local variable to a newly created object, leaving the caller's variable unchanged.) Tj
T*
(If the object is MUTABLE \(list, dict, set\), in-place mutating methods \(e.g.) Tj
